error: 'Pair' cannot be copied between arenas

   ┌─ test/fail/10_copy_type_with_pointer.nul:15:12
   │
 8 │     left:  *Inner
   │            ──────  'Pair' holds a pointer here
   ·
15 │     return arena.copy(p)
   │            ^^^^^^^^^^^^^  this moves the struct, not what 'left' points at
   │
   = note: a copy moves the bytes a value owns directly. A pointer inside would
           keep pointing into the old arena, so the copy would live in 'arena'
           while 'left' did not.
   = help: copy what the pointer reaches, and rebuild the struct around it
             var q = arena.create(Pair)
             q.left = arena.create(Inner)
             q.left.value = p.left.value
             q.count = p.count
